message: "If you use this work, please cite the paper."
title: "Reading the Rows: Five Measurement Defects in an Audit of an Answer Endpoint, and the One Result That Remained"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Theodoro
    given-names: Caio
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-7343-981X"
date-released: 2026-11-23
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24454863
repository-code: "https://github.com/caiotheodoro/titer"
url: "https://huggingface.co/spaces/caiotheodoro/titer"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - benchmark auditing
  - measurement error
  - expertise verification
  - negative results
  - pre-registration
abstract: >-
  A worked case of auditing an answer endpoint's affirmations of claims about named people
  against SEC filings and OpenAlex authorship records. Six headline numbers were produced;
  five were defects of the measurement, each found by reading below the number. The sixth,
  a false-affirmation rate, survived three attacks and is reported with its intervals and
  limits, including an oracle error of unknown size. The code and results are MIT, the paper CC BY 4.0.
